      "body": "## Summary\n- Document that CUDA graphs consume extra GPU memory and can OOM during capture after successful model load.\n- Show how to reduce CUDA graph memory by limiting `cudagraph_capture_sizes`.\n- Add CLI examples for both `--cudagraph-capture-sizes` and `--compilation-config`.\n\n## Why this is not duplicating an existing PR\n- Checked open PRs with:\n  - `gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search 'conserving memory cudagraph capture sizes'`\n  - `gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search 'cudagraph capture sizes memory'`\n- I found related CUDA graph implementation PRs, but no open PR specifically updating the memory conservation docs with these CLI tuning examples.\n\n## Test Plan\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files docs/configuration/conserving_memory.md`\n\n## Notes\n- AI assistance was used to draft this documentation change. The changed lines were reviewed before submission.\n",
